From 8b32e5c95e97cc65d4e4f9fa33876a2c826bbc8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:35:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST Economy 0041: StrikeList, the strike book follows
 the expert list strictly (the user: "literally just follow the list")

New flag StrikeList (off in the bundle). CvStrikePlan gets the expert lists, empty by
default (Personality's rows fill them with AddBuild/AddTech/AddPolicy):
aBuild[] (unit or building class + count, in order), aTech[], aPolicy[].

From strike state PREP to the declaration (IsStrikePending), the capital builds the first
list item still short. Counts add up along the list and count built units (not the
starting ones; upgraded ones and settlers that founded cities count), so a lost unit is
rebuilt in its place. No settler holds, no gold check. Deviations: the city in danger (a
melee defender from the plan), an item the game can't do yet (passed over, logged
LIST WAIT). After the list and in the other cities: the plan's core/support/siege to the
plan's counts (a worker first where a city has none in its area), then more core while
affordable; a late strike in its economy-first PREP uses the regular book. Research and
policies follow the plan's lists (CvTechAI, CvPolicyAI). City log: "STRIKE LIST - ...".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZj2nf4FeZTEHWjvnhhA
